              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this with my oldest boy yesterday as a fruit dip for our New Year's Eve snacking.....I wanted to pretend that we were kind of eating healthy. ;) This was really inexpensive to make because I found the margarita mix at Grocery Outlet and everything else was either on sale for cheap or I had it already in my pantry. I made my own fresh squeezed orange juice and I used Cool Whip for the whipped cream. I also used reduced fat cream cheese and light whipped topping. We loved this, even my husband! We ate sliced organic apples, chunk pineapple, Cutie slices and whole strawberries with this. Next time, I might add some lime zest to this, but that's a personal choice.",
